WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:05.279
Arrows are set to fly when Jeremy Renner's
Hawkeye spin-off series hits the Disney+ streaming

00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:10.900
platform in 2021, but it turns out there was
originally a very different plan for Marvel's

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.220
bow-loving Avenger.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.680
That plan was to give Clint Barton his moment
in the cinematic sun with a feature film in

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:18.900
the vein of the rest of his original Avengers
brethren.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:23.880
Somewhere along the line, though, Marvel head
honcho Kevin Feige had second thoughts about

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.500
continuing Hawkeye's story in a big-screen,
standalone film.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:31.520
Rather than banking on the one-off Hawkeye
flick that Renner had originally signed on

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:36.040
for, Feige and the Marvel team instead reimagined
the hero's narrative prospects for a small

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:40.910
screen venture, deciding that the Hawkeye
story the MCU needed would actually benefit

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:42.460
from a serialized approach.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.980
The Disney+ series will see Renner's arrow-slinging
archer officially passing the torch to the

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.140
next Hawkeye in the form of the comics' fan
favorite character Kate Bishop.

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:55.840
Though no deal has officially been inked for
the coveted role of Kate, Hailee Steinfeld

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:59.780
has been circling the role for months, and
it seems like just a matter of time before

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:00.320
a deal is done.

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:05.460
Although it's plain that a multi-episode serial
will allow for more of a deep dive into Barton's

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:10.340
post-Endgame story than a feature film would
have, Feige was a bit apprehensive about flipping

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:10.880
the plan.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:15.040
Luckily, it doesn't sound like Renner needed
much convincing about transitioning Hawkeye

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.860
from big screen to small.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:22.200
Renner's Hawkeye has been hanging around the
MCU since that brief cameo in 2011's Thor,

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.190
followed by a full appearance in 2012's The
Avengers.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:30.280
The character has appeared in just three MCU
films since: Avengers: Age of Ultron, Captain

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:32.260
America: Civil War, and Avengers: Endgame.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:36.700
While Barton has become a fan favorite of
sorts over the course of those films, he's

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:42.130
frequently been relegated to secondary status
among the increasingly crowded Avengers landscape.

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:44.940
"We haven't met yet.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.020
I'm Clint."

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:48.160
"I don't care."

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:52.120
This likely played a big part in Hawkeye's
transition to the small screen.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:56.759
Of course, if the ultimate goal of Marvel's
Hawkeye series is to see Barton pass the bow

00:01:56.759 --> 00:02:01.840
to the next generation, then the series should
also offer an opportunity for MCU fans to

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:03.560
get acquainted with young Kate Bishop.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:08.300
The inclusion of Bishop in future phases of
the MCU also helps to bolster the rumor that

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:12.720
Feige and company are planning for a Young
Avengers flick at some point in the future.

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:18.240
One other Young Avenger has already been introduced
in the MCU: the now-teenage Cassie Lang, the

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:22.669
daughter of Ant-Man, who in the comics goes
on to be a member of the Young Avengers under

00:02:22.669 --> 00:02:23.720
the name Stature.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:28.180
It's just possible that the Hawkeye series
could set up the formation of this team, although

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:30.330
that is pure speculation at this point.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:34.780
In fact, it's still a bit too early to tell
just what narrative tack Hawkeye will take,

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:39.069
but it seems likely that we'll be seeing a
modified version of Bishop's origin story.

00:02:39.069 --> 00:02:43.489
The character first appeared as a trauma survivor
who beefs up on combat training in the wake

00:02:43.489 --> 00:02:44.420
of a brutal attack.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:49.700
She's thrust into heroic action by happenstance,
coming to the aid of the titular team in Young

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:50.440
Avengers #1.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:54.800
By the time Bishop took up the Hawkeye mantle
in the comics, Barton had already been killed

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:55.340
off.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:59.240
Strangely enough, it was Captain America,
by way of Jessica Jones, who officially passed

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:04.220
the Hawkeye code name off to Bishop, so Marvel's
creative team will clearly have to make some

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:06.960
changes when adapting Bishop's story for the
small screen.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:09.840
That, however, should be a fairly easy task.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:13.960
Given the wringer that Barton was put through
during the events of Avengers: Endgame, it's

00:03:13.969 --> 00:03:18.349
a safe bet that the aging hero will be eager
to pass the bow on to a young apprentice.

00:03:18.349 --> 00:03:21.860
Whatever direction Marvel's creative team
choose to go in with Hawkeye, it's clear that

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:25.080
the narrative ground for the series remains
more than fertile.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:29.740
It's just as clear that fans are beyond excited
to spend a little extra time with Barton;

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:34.160
here's hoping that the excitement extends
to whomever steps into the fray as Bishop.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:38.600
Hawkeye is expected to debut on Disney+ in
late 2021.

